+### Kimi rows in the capability table (2026-10-27, E5.6 of `todo/PLAN_vibe_and_kimi_runtimes_E5.md`)
+
+The table has three `kimi` rows, in `shared/runtime-capabilities.json` and in the seed's `runtimes` list: `none` and `disk` are `unconfined`, and `web` is `unmeasured`.
+`none` is `unconfined`, not `confined`, because Kimi's `Grep` and `Glob` read files outside the working folder (RESULTS_kimi_confinement.md §9, M-K6), so the
+row is admitted FLAGGED as "Can read this machine". `disk` is `unconfined` for the same reason, and its branch's AGENTS.md, skills, sub-agents and `.mcp.json`
+load from disk (M-K9), so the roots are COPIED into the snapshot and never granted. The `web` row is refused, and its sentence names
+`research/RESULTS_kimi_confinement.md`, because no Kimi cell measures a web tool. The rows' `date` is `2026-10-13` for every cell.
+The planner arm `"kimi" => Kimi(grant, flag)` in `ConfinementPlanner.Fragments` puts NO flag on any capability: Kimi's confinement is the shim's (D15), not its argv.
+`disk` is a snapshot of the roots; `none` is an empty scratch folder; `web` never reaches the arm.
+`RuntimeCapabilities.Runtimes` (`src_mcp/core/QuestionConsult/RuntimeCapabilities.cs`) is a hand-written list, not read from the seed. A row for a runtime outside it
+breaks the file, so adding `kimi` to the seed means adding it there too, and the generated `src_vs_code/src/runtimeCapabilities.generated.ts` is written by its generator.
+`KimiConsultant.Build` refuses any plan that has `Leading`, `Flags` or `AddDirs`, with the sentence "a Kimi row's confinement is the shim's; a plan with flags is not one coai made for kimi".
+
